<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry VI, Holy Roman Emperor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1165">1165</a>–1197</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry VI was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a> emperor, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a>, crowned emperor in 1191. Through his wife Constance he won the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> in 1194. He held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-i-of-england">Richard I of England</a> for ransom and raised the Lusignans to the kingship of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a> as imperial <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a>. His sudden death in 1197 led to a disputed succession in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-vi-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="Henry VI, Holy Roman Emperor" width="320" height="690" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Peter of Eboli · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:JindrichVIStauf_trun.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>At the Diet of Schwäbisch Hall in 1190 Emperor <b>Henry VI</b> confirmed that the ducal rank applied to Henry's own territories, which included Louvain, Brussels, Antwerp and lands stretching north towards the Meuse, rather than to the whole of Lower Lorraine.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-brabant">Duchy of Brabant · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The decisive step came during the contest for the German throne that followed the death of Emperor <b>Henry VI</b>: in 1198 Duke Ottokar I backed Philip of Swabia, who recognised him as king.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-bohemia">Kingdom of Bohemia · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Henry VI of Hohenstaufen</b> conquered the kingdom in 1194, and his son Frederick II defended it against the papacy, using Muslim soldiers from Lucera.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-sicily">Kingdom of Sicily · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Prince Levon II, with the support of the emperors Frederick Barbarossa and <b>Henry VI</b>, was crowned in the cathedral of Tarsus on 6 January 1198, the Armenian Christmas, by the Catholicos Gregory VI Abirad.</blockquote><a href="/essays/christmas-day-in-history">Christmas Day in History</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1191 the Romans, with <b>Emperor Henry VI</b>'s consent, destroyed the town.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-tusculum">County of Tusculum</a></li><li><blockquote>At the Diet of Schwäbisch Hall in 1190 <b>Emperor Henry VI</b> limited the duke's authority to his own lands, and the Louvain dukes thereafter ruled as dukes of Brabant, keeping the title duke of Lothier.</blockquote><a href="/state/duchy-of-lower-lorraine">Duchy of Lower Lorraine</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nijmegen">Nijmegen</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/netherlands">the Netherlands</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/messina">Messina</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=51.85,5.86&amp;year=1185" aria-label="Nijmegen on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4682 371 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Henry VI, Holy Roman Emperor"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5132 641h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5132 641h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=51.85,5.86&amp;year=1185">What was here in 1185? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
